# 3md files are Markdown with a Z axis, but GitHub's Markdown preview joins a
# single newline into a space. That turns a blob into one paragraph, so the
# planes in gdscript/examples/grove/scene.3md read as one line. Show the source
# instead. Forcing Text also stops Linguist from calling leading-dot ASCII
# grids Roff (troff macros start with a dot).
*.3md linguist-language=Text

# The example corpus is sample content, not source - keep it out of language stats.
Examples/** linguist-documentation

# The generated bundles concatenate every doc into one file. As Markdown, GitHub
# renders them as a single condensed run-together wall (the `@plane`/`---` lines
# do not map to headings). They are viewer artifacts, not meant to be read on
# GitHub, so show them as plain text (readable source, banner first) and mark
# them generated. The viewer still loads them fine.
docs.3md linguist-generated linguist-language=Text
web/docs.3md linguist-generated linguist-language=Text
web/examples-gallery.3md linguist-generated linguist-language=Text

# Generated/vendored artifacts: don't count toward language stats.
web/gifs/** linguist-generated
web/assets/three-md.js linguist-generated
conformance/** linguist-documentation
